@top Emacsvox

Welcome to the Emacsvox user manual.  Begin with the introduction, follow the
installation path until Emacsvox speaks, and then try the guided first session
in Basic Usage.  Platform and compatibility detail is available in Speech
Backends when you need it.  Exact commands, options, and keymaps are in the
separate
@ref{Top,Emacsvox Reference Manual,,emacsvox-reference,Emacsvox Reference
Manual}.  Selected historical Emacspeak material is in the separate
@ref{Top,Emacspeak Heritage,,emacsvox-heritage,Emacspeak Heritage} manual and
is not current setup guidance.  For rapidly evolving development and Aural
Presentation rule-authoring details, also consult @file{Readme.org} and
@file{etc/aural-presentation-reference.org} in the source tree.

